From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Michael Niedermayer <michael@niedermayer.cc>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 07:33:05 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] avformat/oggenc: Reset the current page when it cannot be
 buffered

On allocation failure the full page stayed in the stream context, and
the next segment was added past its 255 entry segment table.

Fixes: out of array access
Fixes: flOsaBhTFc6F
Fixes: AISLE-2026-0111-00072
Negative size memset Replicated through API with ASAN and av_max_alloc() lowered after the header
Found-by: Joshua Rogers <joshua.rogers@aisle.com>

(cherry picked from commit 6d40aa17395aaba80922441bcfb58399a88475e3)
---
 libavformat/oggenc.c | 4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/libavformat/oggenc.c b/libavformat/oggenc.c
index 5c7e3da..cee9c01 100644
--- a/libavformat/oggenc.c
+++ b/libavformat/oggenc.c
@@ -192,8 +192,10 @@ static int ogg_buffer_page(AVFormatContext *s, OGGStreamContext *oggstream)
     OGGPageList **p = &ogg->page_list;
     OGGPageList *l = av_mallocz(sizeof(*l));
 
-    if (!l)
+    if (!l) {
+        ogg_reset_cur_page(oggstream);
         return AVERROR(ENOMEM);
+    }
     l->page = oggstream->page;
 
     oggstream->page.start_granule = ogg_granule_to_timestamp(oggstream, oggstream->page.granule);
